    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116498" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦχρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὁ</span> (cf. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			2.39
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>paleness,
			wanness,</i> esp. <i>the pale hue</i> of fear, once in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦχρός τέ μιν εἷλε παρειάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.35
				</span></i>
			; also in <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>JTr.</u>
				1
			</span></i> (adapting <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>) and late Poets, as An drom. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.258
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Paul.Sil.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>birds' pease, Lathyrus Ochrus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				301
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				627b17
			</span></i>(pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				8.3.1
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>CP</u>
				4.2.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				2.139
			</span></i>.</div>
